# marks.walk (order 1581): the bench's mark guard and its positive
# control. A Bench open asks the home no mark (1562: the bench's arrivals
# never were the home's, `loquax_m9::home::route` keeps their marks on the
# board); a real chat's open does, or the guard's silence proves nothing.
# Both are read in the bench home's own log (mailbox.log, `expect home`).
#
# The real chat with an unread message comes first, the newest on the
# list: the fixture's own unread are read after the first walk that
# opened them, so the control makes its own. Right before the walk:
#
#   bash scripts/m9-bench-home.sh send "mark control"
#   bash scripts/m9-walk.sh --rig <rig> --walk scripts/m9-walks/marks.walk [--image <bench elf>]
#
# and the walk waits for the board to pull it (row 0 is the newest chat).

wait page=chats
sleep 15000
row 0

# The control: the sender's chat opened, its message read on screen for
# the dwell; the board asks its home a read mark.
key enter
wait page=chat
expect home "HOME mark"
key back
wait page=chats

# The guard: an arrival in Bench, Bench opened; the home hears nothing.
bench arrive
key enter
wait page=chat
expect no home "HOME mark"
key back
wait page=chats
